From b57e38b4e450c6b87d844d02cb5b9f8c37cf464f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 17:05:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Enforce the occupant invariant, report a time loss as one,
 and ship a CSP

- Occupants are eight frozen shared values (occupantOf); clonePosition and
  boardAfter copy arrays only. A write throws. 1.2x on the depth-4 search,
  perft to depth 5 and 11,944 differential positions unchanged.
- The dead throwaway-clone parameter is gone; DECISIONS.md now says the
  repetition map is still copied per node and the search still slows with
  game length (1.9x at 150 entries).
- A flag is reported as a time loss, not a resignation; the clock stops
  when the opponent drops; a takeback restarts the mover's clock, resets
  the animation counter and restarts the bot worker.
- The peer path stores the engine's action object, not the peer's.
- Both pages carry a meta CSP; test/security.test.js guards it and the
  no-innerHTML rule. CACHE v41 -> v42.
